    "narrative": "The Austin Waves\u2019 offensive outlook for June 10 is anchored by high-ceiling matchups against middle-tier pitching, led by **Gunnar Henderson** (80.62) and **Jackson Merrill** (75.27). **Gunnar Henderson** is our premier play, benefiting from a significant park factor boost and a strategic advantage against the slow delivery of George Kirby, which elevates his stolen base potential\u2014the lifeblood of our 5x5 strategy. Similarly, **Jackson Merrill** draws a favorable matchup against Singer, where a strong platoon advantage and wind conditions pushing toward the outfield fences amplify his power-speed profile. We are also leaning on **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (61.56), who, despite the threat of a tough arm in Luzardo, retains strong lineup utility and a dynamic platoon lift to remain a staple in our UTIL slot.\n\nThe most difficult decision for today\u2019s lineup involved the benching of **Coby Mayo** (47.61). While **Coby Mayo** benefits from the same favorable park environment as **Gunnar Henderson**, his projected platoon disadvantage against a right-handed starter suppresses his floor compared to the consistency offered by **Nolan Schanuel** and **Josh Jung**. We are keeping a close eye on the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Liam Hicks**, **Nolan Schanuel**, **Josh Jung**, **Kyle Tucker**, **Dominic Smith**, **Andy Pages**, and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**; should any of these hitters drop in the batting order upon official confirmation, their projected scores\u2014which currently rely heavily on premium spots like #1 or #2\u2014will require re-evaluation. While **Nasim Nunez** (56.32) remains a viable start due to his switch-hitting versatility, we are wary of his lower slot in the order against Ray, though his presence ensures we maintain our necessary SB velocity to compete in the category.",
